readme.excerpt:
An experimental C++ extension for stock DuckDB 2.0 that adds versioning to ordinary DuckDB databases: snapshots, time travel, branches, clones, restore and S3 export. Native catalogs, SQL, transactions, indexes and compression run unchanged over a durable differential filesystem that shares unchanged data between all versions. The SQL surface follows DuckLake's conventions.

INSTALL differential FROM community; LOAD differential; ATTACH 'differential:sales' AS sales; -- created on first use CREATE TABLE sales.t AS SELECT 42 AS value; CALL differential create snapshot('sales', name = 'baseline', message = 'initial load'); UPDATE sales.t SET value = 99; ATTACH 'differential:sales' AS old (SNAPSHOT NAME 'baseline'); SELECT value FROM old.t; -- 42 SELECT value FROM sales.t AT (VERSION = 1); -- 42, DuckLake-style time travel FROM sales.snapshots();

Status: experimental Build from source and load the local artifact (development); community installation commands describe the planned release. Full v1 acceptance is not complete. Only macOS arm64 and a MinIO S3 endpoint are fully tested; real AWS was exercised manually (exports, reads, branch heads), and other platforms are untested.
